Prompt: What is SE and how to compute to get its values in the image?<IMG>v2_492_0.jpg
Response: SE stands for Standard Error. It is a measure of the amount of variation or dispersion of a set of values. To compute the SE for the given data, you would take the average of the squares of the standard deviations (SD) for each parameter (SPH, CYL, AX) and then take the square root of that average.
